===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|Πύθων||lang=grc}}, the name of the mythological enormous serpent at Delphi slain by Apollo, from {{term|Πῡθώ|lang=grc}}, the early name of Delphi, from {{term|πυθώ||to rot, to decay|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθɑːn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A type of large [[constrict]]ing [[snake]].

